      <h1>AI method: recorded run, failed attempt and limits</h1>
      <p>
        The retained private store contains one completed extraction run for one
        C-014 source document. It is not evidence of an absolute historical
        provider-request figure, so none is published.
      </p>

      <h2>Completed run</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Uncached input tokens</dt><dd>3</dd>
        <dt>Cached input tokens</dt><dd>17,682</dd>
        <dt>Output tokens</dt><dd>1,053</dd>
        <dt>Recorded cost</dt><dd>USD 0.00161784</dd>
        <dt>Recorded latency</dt><dd>10,017 ms</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
        The cache read shows that a prefix was reused. The request which primed
        the cache is unestablished; no origin or historical request total is
        inferred.
      </p>

      <h2>Failed attempt on 13 August 2026</h2>
      <p>
        A later authorized request returned an incomplete response. The adapter
        rejected it as <code>provider_response_incomplete</code>. It produced no
        stored extraction run and no stored claim.
      </p>
      <p>
        The adapter was subsequently corrected so a future authorized call can
        preserve content-free usage, cost, latency, incomplete reason and
        rejection details while still failing closed. That correction does not
        reconstruct the missing accounting or establish the cause of the failed
        attempt.
      </p>

      <h2>What has and has not been demonstrated</h2>
      <p>
        The current recorded repository suite passes 169 tests covering schemas,
        storage, evidence and publication gates, adapter behavior, static export
        and leak scans. Engineering tests do not measure model extraction quality.
      </p>
      <p>
        No accuracy, precision or recall result exists. The scored golden set is
        empty, so there is no basis for an extraction-quality percentage or a
        comparative model claim.
      </p>
    </main>
